From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: macos: refuse MAP_BLOB of a resource that is
 already mapped

A second RESOURCE_MAP_BLOB at another offset succeeded and overwrote
shmem_offset, orphaning the first hv_vm_map. UNMAP_BLOB then removed
only the second mapping, and RESOURCE_UNREF, seeing no mapping left,
munmapped the host pages the hypervisor still mapped into the guest
at the first offset. Linux's virtio-gpu maps a blob once; reject the
second map instead.
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
index ef9e9af..de5eebd 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
@@ -1317,6 +1317,17 @@ impl VirtioGpu {
         shm_region: &VirtioShmRegion,
         offset: u64,
     ) -> VirtioGpuResult {
+        // A second MAP_BLOB of a mapped resource would orphan the first guest mapping:
+        // UNMAP_BLOB only removes the last one, and UNREF would then munmap host pages
+        // the hypervisor still maps into the guest.
+        if self
+            .resources
+            .get(&resource_id)
+            .is_some_and(|r| r.shmem_offset.is_some())
+        {
+            error!("resource {resource_id}: already mapped into the guest");
+            return Err(ErrUnspec);
+        }
         let map_info = self.rutabaga.map_info(resource_id).map_err(|_| ErrUnspec)?;
         let mapping = self.blob_host_mapping(resource_id)?;
         let resource = self
